Nodes 3
Tiers 2
Podsize 3

# One leaf switch with three directly attached RNIC nodes and one uplink to
# each of the three spine switches. Every experiment in this study is
# same-leaf, so the spines carry no traffic: the measured fabric is a single
# switch hop, and a same-leaf pair reproduces it exactly. Three nodes is the
# smallest node count that still expresses a 2 to 1 fan-in.
#
# The rate is the profile goodput asymptote rounded to whole Gbit/s, which is
# what the loader parses and what the runtime requires -link_bps to match.
# 515 ns per hop puts a 2 B message's round trip (four pipe traversals plus
# four store-and-forward serializations) at 2.081 us, the measured floor.
Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 97
Radix_Down 3
Radix_Up 3
Downlink_Latency_ns 515
Switch_Latency_ns 0

# Three spine switches, each with one link to the leaf.
Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 97
Radix_Down 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 515
Switch_Latency_ns 0
